/*
ReserveBuckets Reserve meter buckets (all-or-nothing)

Reserve a set of meter buckets in one all-or-nothing call. The engine's three-way
outcome is returned verbatim:

- `allowed` — the held set is persisted for the matching `/commit` and its
  `reservation_id` is returned.
- `denied` — a semantic refusal (unknown/disabled meter, exhausted allowance/quota).
  Fail-closed. Carries an `upgrade` offer when a reachable plan would unblock it. A meter
  that bills overage up to a cap and has no room left for the estimate is denied with
  `overage_cap_reached`.
- `indeterminate` — a dependency was down; the deployment's infra policy decided
  admit/refuse and the reason is surfaced.

A meter that requires an agreement the customer has not accepted denies the whole set with
`reason: agreement_required`, the `meter` and `blocked`.

Note: the HTTP status is always `200` — the decision is in the `outcome` field.


 @param ctx context.Context - for authentication, logging, cancellation, deadlines, tracing, etc. Passed from http.Request or context.Background().
 @return ApiReserveBucketsRequest
*/
